From 1111111111111111111111111111111111111111 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Tia <anthropic@jetm.me>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] rzv2h-dev: boot Avocado extlinux from SD, not vendor
 ext4/booti

The Avocado image (stone) provisions a FAT boot partition carrying
extlinux.conf, the kernel Image and the RDK dtb, plus an erofs rootfs
addressed by PARTUUID. The vendor CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND instead runs
`ext4load mmc 0:2 boot/Image` + booti against a single ext4 rootfs with a
fixed EVK dtb name, so it cannot boot the Avocado layout at all.

Point CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND at sysboot (CONFIG_CMD_SYSBOOT, already enabled)
to parse extlinux.conf on the FAT boot partition (partition 1), trying
mmc 1 then mmc 0 so it does not depend on which controller the microSD
enumerates on. The kernel/fdt/ramdisk load addresses match the vendor
booti (kernel 0x48080000, fdt 0x48000000); scriptaddr sits inside the
0x48000000-0x58000000 bootm window.

Build-verified only: the sysboot path/prefix, mmc index and load
addresses are board-specific and must be confirmed at the u-boot prompt
on real hardware.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Avocado board integration]
Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <anthropic@jetm.me>
---
 include/configs/rzv2h-dev.h | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/configs/rzv2h-dev.h b/include/configs/rzv2h-dev.h
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/include/configs/rzv2h-dev.h
+++ b/include/configs/rzv2h-dev.h
@@ -80,7 +80,11 @@
 	"bootcmd_check=if mmc dev 1; then run sd1load; else run sd0load; fi \0"
 #endif
 
-#define CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND	"env default -a;run bootcmd_check;run bootimage"
+#define CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND \
+	"setenv scriptaddr 0x50000000; setenv kernel_addr_r 0x48080000; " \
+	"setenv fdt_addr_r 0x48000000; setenv ramdisk_addr_r 0x4a000000; " \
+	"sysboot mmc 1:1 any ${scriptaddr} /extlinux/extlinux.conf; " \
+	"sysboot mmc 0:1 any ${scriptaddr} /extlinux/extlinux.conf"
 
 /* For board */
 /* Ethernet RAVB */
